Subarrays with sum K: Given an unsorted array arr[] of integers, find the number of subarrays whose sum exactly equal to a given number k.

Explanation:

so in this question we have ot find the number of subarrays where sum of the numbers inside is equal to k;
but we are not going to use 2 points cause this contains negative numbers aswell..
SO we are going to use prefix sum. In the hasmap instead of storing array numbers, we store the prefixsum of the num and its frequemcy.
we search for the complement of the prefixsum in the hashmap and if it exists we increase the total numberof counts


Code:
class Solution {
    public int cntSubarrays(int[] arr, int k) {
        // code here
        HashMap<Integer,Integer> map = new HashMap<>();
        int prefixSum=0; int count=0;
        map.put(0,1);
        for(int num:arr){
            prefixSum+=num;
            int neededSum=prefixSum-k;
            
            if(map.containsKey(neededSum)){
                count+=map.get(neededSum);
            }
            
            map.put(prefixSum,map.getOrDefault(prefixSum,0)+1);
        }
        return count;
    }
}
